<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Washington Naval Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1921">1921</a>–<a href="/years/1922">1922</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Washington Naval Conference was an international meeting held in Washington from November 1921 to February 1922 on naval disarmament and the Pacific. Its treaties limited the battleship fleets of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, replaced the Anglo-Japanese Alliance and guaranteed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s territorial integrity. In related agreements Japan returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shandong">Shandong</a> to China and Britain promised to give back Weihaiwei.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/washington-naval-conference.jpg" alt="Washington Naval Conference" width="320" height="235" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Harris &amp; Ewing, photographer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Conference_on_Limitation_of_Armaments,_Washington,_D.C..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
